  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But in order that what I have said may be made evident, I shall explain the interchange of the generations.",
    "chunk_index": 33,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If we reckon the generations from David through Solomon, Matthan is found to be the third from the end, who begat Jacob the father of Joseph.",
    "chunk_index": 34,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But if, with Luke, we reckon them from Nathan the son of David, in like manner the third from the end is Melchi, whose son was Heli the father of Joseph.",
    "chunk_index": 35,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For Joseph was the son of Heli, the son of Melchi.",
    "chunk_index": 36,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "As Joseph, therefore, is the object proposed to us, we have to show how it is that each is represented as his father, both Jacob as descending from Solomon, and Heli as descending from Nathan:",
    "chunk_index": 37,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "first, how these two, Jacob and Heli, were brothers; and then also how the fathers of these, Matthan and Melchi, being of different families, are shown to be the grandfathers of Joseph.",
    "chunk_index": 38,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Well, then, Matthan and Melchi, having taken the same woman to wife in succession, begat children who were uterine brothers, as the law did not prevent a widow, whether such by divorce or by the death of her husband, from marrying another.",
    "chunk_index": 39,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "By Estha, then—for such is her name according to tradition—Matthan first, the descendant of Solomon, begets Jacob;",
    "chunk_index": 40,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and on Matthan’s death, Melchi, who traces his descent back to Nathan, being of the same tribe but of another family, having married her, as has been already said, had a son Heli.",
    "chunk_index": 41,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s10",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Thus, then, we shall find Jacob and Heli uterine brothers, though of different families.",
    "chunk_index": 42,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s11",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And of these, the one Jacob having taken the wife of his brother Heli, who died childless, begat by her the third, Joseph—his son by nature and by account.",
    "chunk_index": 43,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s12",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s12",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Whence also it is written, “And Jacob begat Joseph.” But according to law he was the son of Heli, for Jacob his brother raised up seed to him.",
    "chunk_index": 44,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s13",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s13",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Wherefore also the genealogy deduced through him will not be made void, which the Evangelist Matthew in his enumeration gives thus: “And Jacob begat Joseph.”",
    "chunk_index": 45,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s14",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s14",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But Luke, on the other hand, says, “Who was the son, as was supposed (for this, too, he adds), of Joseph, the son of Heli, the son of Melchi.”",
    "chunk_index": 46,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.III.1.s15",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.III.1.s15",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For it was not possible more distinctly to state the generation according to law; and thus in this mode of generation he has entirely omitted the word “begat” to the very end, carrying back the genealogy by way of conclusion to Adam and to God.",
    "chunk_index": 47,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "IV.",
    "chunk_index": 48,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Nor indeed is this incapable of proof, neither is it a rash conjecture.",
    "chunk_index": 49,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For the kinsmen of the Saviour after the flesh, whether to magnify their own origin or simply to state the fact, but at all events speaking truth, have also handed down the following account:",
    "chunk_index": 50,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Some Idumean robbers attacking Ascalon, a city of Palestine, besides other spoils which they took from a temple of Apollo,",
    "chunk_index": 51,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "which was built near the walls, carried off captive one Antipater, son of a certain Herod, a servant of the temple.",
    "chunk_index": 52,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And as the priest was not able to pay the ransom for his son, Antipater was brought up in the customs of the Idumeans, and afterwards enjoyed the friendship of Hyrcanus, the high priest of Judea.",
    "chunk_index": 53,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And being sent on an embassy to Pompey on behalf of Hyrcanus, and having restored to him the kingdom which was being wasted by Aristobulus his brother, he was so fortunate as to obtain the title of procurator of Palestine.",
    "chunk_index": 54,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And when Antipater was treacherously slain through envy of his great good fortune, his son Herod succeeded him, who was afterwards appointed king of Judea under Antony and Augustus by a decree of the senate.",
    "chunk_index": 55,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.IV.1.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "His sons were Herod and the other tetrarchs. These accounts are given also in the histories of the Greeks.",
    "chunk_index": 56,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "V.",
    "chunk_index": 57,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V.1.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But as up to that time the genealogies of the Hebrews had been registered in the public archives, and those, too, which were traced back to the proselytes—as,",
    "chunk_index": 58,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V.1.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for example, to Achior the Ammanite, and Ruth the Moabitess, and those who left Egypt along with the Israelites, and intermarried with them—Herod,",
    "chunk_index": 59,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V.1.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "knowing that the lineage of the Israelites contributed nothing to him, and goaded by the consciousness of his ignoble birth, burned the registers of their families.",
    "chunk_index": 60,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V.1.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "This he did, thinking that he would appear to be of noble birth, if no one else could trace back his descent by the public register to the patriarchs or proselytes, and to that mixed race called georæ.",
    "chunk_index": 61,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V.1.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "A few, however, of the studious, having private records of their own, either by remembering the names or by getting at them in some other way from the archives, pride themselves in preserving the memory of their noble descent;",
    "chunk_index": 62,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V.1.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and among these happen to be those already mentioned, called desposyni, on account of their connection with the family of the Saviour.",
    "chunk_index": 63,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V.1.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And these coming from Nazara and Cochaba, Judean villages, to other parts of the country, set forth the above-named genealogy as accurately as possible from the Book of Days.",
    "chunk_index": 64,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
    "canonical_ref": "Afric.EpArist.V.1.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Whether, then, the case stand thus or not, no one could discover a more obvious explanation, according to my own opinion and that of any sound judge.",
    "chunk_index": 65,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 225,
    "date_range": [
      220,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides#Afric.EpArist.V.1.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/africanus-epistle-to-aristides",
